  "aiSummary": "This bill requires North Carolina's Department of Veterans and Military Affairs to improve maintenance at the state's four veterans cemeteries by addressing specific issues like delayed headstone installation, grounds damage, and poor appearance. It also directs the department to review and potentially adjust policies around funeral services at these cemeteries, with findings due to the General Assembly by October 1, 2025.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue that veterans and their families deserve well-maintained cemeteries that honor their service and sacrifice. The bill addresses documented problems including delayed headstone installation, grounds damage from equipment, drainage issues, and poor overall appearance. Allowing volunteer groups like the VFW and military organizations to help with maintenance provides additional resources while enabling veterans to serve their community.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may be concerned about the cost of implementing these improvements and whether the Department of Veterans and Military Affairs has adequate budget and staffing to meet these requirements. Some may question whether relaxing policies on funeral services (chapel-only rules, attendance limits, visitation restrictions) could create operational challenges or safety concerns at cemetery facilities, or whether the October 2025 deadline allows sufficient time for meaningful policy review.",
